**Related Spec**: specs/241-wait-for-retained-active-workers-instead-of-exiting-execute/

# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs
#
# Generated from: specs/249-make-execute-resume-active-issue-state-safely/requirements.md
Feature: Make execute resume active issue state safely
  The execute controller previously treated a transient idle worker without a
  handoff as missing_handoff, then resumed a later issue's review from main.
  This was fixed by waiting once for settlement and restoring the active issue
  branch before incomplete post-start steps.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Transient idle does not end a worker step
    Given a retained matching worker is idle without a handoff and later writes a valid passed handoff
    When the controller observes that worker
    Then it does not record missing_handoff, start a duplicate, or close the pane during the wait
    And it accepts the validated handoff and continues the queue

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Explicit unsafe outcomes still fail closed
    Given a worker is failed, blocked, intervention-required, malformed, mismatched, or genuinely stalled
    When the controller evaluates the worker and its handoff
    Then it stops the queue, keeps the relevant pane open, and records the specific reasonCode

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Resume restores the active issue branch
    Given an earlier queue issue is fully delivered and a later issue has completed start and implement
    When /sdlc-execute resumes the persisted queue
    Then it checks out and validates the later issue branch before launching the next incomplete worker

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Review cannot compare main against main
    Given the next incomplete step is review1 or review2 and the worktree is still on the default branch
    When the controller prepares the review
    Then it stops with review_branch_mismatch or branch_checkout_failed before sending /review

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Serial resume remains non-destructive
    Given a clean resumable queue or a dirty tree that the existing issues[0] safety contract already governs
    When branch recovery and worker settlement run
    Then the controller does not stash, reset, or discard user work and does not reorder the persisted queue

  # --- Combined Regression ---

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Combined transient-idle then delivered-prefix resume reaches review from the issue branch
    Given fixtures model a transient idle implement worker that later writes a passed handoff
    And an earlier delivered issue plus a later issue completed through implement
    When the focused controller tests run
    Then the later issue's review starts only after its issue branch is current
    And existing failed, blocked, intervention, and dirty-worktree tests still pass
